1
00:05:54,545 --> 00:06:00,545
Harrison's Flowers is a drama, romance, war film directed by Élie Chouraqui.

2
00:11:49,090 --> 00:11:55,090
Harrison Lloyd, a renowned photojournalist covering the
war in Yugoslavia, is reported missing.

3
00:17:43,636 --> 00:17:49,636
Sarah, his wife, convinced that he is not dead,
decides to go to Bosnia to find him.

4
00:23:38,181 --> 00:23:44,181
Sarah Lloyd, played by Andie MacDowell.

5
00:29:32,727 --> 00:29:38,727
Yeager Pollack, played by Elias Koteas.

6
00:35:27,272 --> 00:35:33,272
Marc Stevenson, played by Brendan Gleeson.

7
00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
Kyle Morris, played by Adrien Brody.

8
00:47:16,363 --> 00:47:22,363
Harrison Lloyd, played by David Strathairn.

9
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
Margaux Lloyd, played by Quinn Shephard.

10
00:59:05,454 --> 00:59:11,454
Harrison's Flowers (French: Les Fleurs d'Harrison) is a 2000
war-romance drama film directed by Elie Chouraqui.

11
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
It stars, among others, Andie MacDowell, Elias Koteas, Brendan Gleeson, Adrien
Brody, Marie Trintignant, Gerard Butler and David Strathairn.

12
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
The film is also Quinn Shephard's big screen debut.

13
01:16:49,090 --> 01:16:55,090
The film premiered at the 2000 San Sebastián International Film Festival,
and released in theatres on 24 January 2001 in France.

14
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
Universal Pictures gave the film a limited theatrical release in the United States on 15 March
2002, then Lionsgate released this film in the United States on DVD in 2007.

15
01:28:38,181 --> 01:28:44,181
For this film's United States version, the film's length was reduced by about
5 minutes; it also features a new score by Cliff Eidelman.

16
01:34:32,727 --> 01:34:38,727
The film only grossed $3 million in worldwide box office against $8 million
production budget, and the overall critical reaction to the film was mixed.

17
01:40:27,272 --> 01:40:33,272
However, Adrien Brody said that this film helped him to be cast in the leading role of
The Pianist (2002), for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor.

18
01:46:21,818 --> 01:46:27,818
Kino Lorber Studio Classics released the film for the
first time on Blu-ray on November 26, 2024.

19
01:52:16,363 --> 01:52:22,363
There is a factual error in this film: the character played by Adrien Brody says that
Croats are Orthodox and Serbs are Catholic, without being contradicted.

20
01:58:10,909 --> 01:58:16,909
The film explores themes of war crimes, balkan war, genocide, missing person.

21
02:04:05,454 --> 02:04:11,454
The tone is emotional.
